{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3309","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3309","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3309\",\"parent_revision\":\"21cc7d69ad55317855ac767f67a466b2b8fe3153399f13f543c9ea5b5ac885a3\",\"root_revision\":\"21cc7d69ad55317855ac767f67a466b2b8fe3153399f13f543c9ea5b5ac885a3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need this serves: keep `backlog_core/search.py`'s full-text search filter from doing avoidable per-item work as the backlog list grows.\\n\\n**Observed**: `_item_matches_term()` (search.py:68) calls `_re.compile(pattern_str, _re.IGNORECASE)` once per item inside `apply_search_filter`'s per-item loop, instead of compiling each regex term once before the loop starts. CPython's `re` module internally caches compiled patterns (up to 512 entries keyed by pattern+flags), so this is a cache-dict lookup per item rather than a true recompile \u2014 not a correctness or scaling blocker today, just redundant lookups.\\n\\n**Fix direction (from review, not prescriptive)**: hoist the compile out of `_item_matches_term`, e.g. compile once in `apply_search_filter` and pass the `Pattern` object down to the per-item predicate.\\n\\n**Related**: `find_content_duplicates()` (search.py:652) has a similar redundant-recomputation pattern \u2014 it calls `apply_search_filter(live_candidates, query)` and then, in the following list comprehension, calls `_build_haystack(c)` again for every matched candidate to compute `match_count`, rebuilding a string `apply_search_filter` already built internally per item during predicate evaluation. Bounded by matched-candidate count, not unbounded growth. Could be avoided by having `apply_search_filter` optionally return `(item, haystack)` pairs, or scoring inline during the filter pass.\\n\\n**Source**: Both findings surfaced during the multi-perspective performance review of #3169 (content-based duplicate detection), verdict APPROVE with these two MINOR findings noted as non-blocking cleanup.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Multi-perspective review follow-up on #3169 (performance perspective, review-3169-20260829T020754Z)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"34a94211664922e08b4bc8fa740a93ec4dc6ecdf6ae88a338bf62d46a42fd1fc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5adg\"}"}